{
 "_readme": [
  "Bot gate on the current build (index.html of this repo, same physics as the shipped main build), run 15/11/2026 with levels6/tools/gate-bot.js, N=2 seeds per bot (seeds 800 + 37000k + L). On most levels the seed changes nothing physical, so both seeds repeat one result: read each bot as one deterministic plan, not as a sample.",
  "Bots: expert = the level's stored solution (sol/solW) + 'hit what still stands' cleanup; sensible = follows the level's bot hints (a tip-reader); naive = all TNT at once on the front-middle ground members; lesson = the plan WITHOUT the level's lesson (must fail on lesson levels). The bots place TNT through the test API (not the tap UI), with the game's real wave/rest rules.",
  "pct = final clear % of the target (PASS 85). failCodes: pct = below 85 %, ~pct = below 85 % with TNT unused, collateral = a protected building over 5 % damage (fails even at a high clear %).",
  "allRuns pools every bot run of the level: passPct, bestClear, medianClear; nearLose80to84 = runs that ended at 80-84 % clear; nearWin85to88 = runs that passed at 85-88 %.",
  "Gate targets (blast-level-standard skill, docs/LEVEL-STANDARD.md): expert wins every seed with margin >= +3; sensible: Normal/Relief/Tutorial wins, Hard/Boss <= 50 %; naive fails from L3; lesson-less fails on lesson levels. Problems the gate itself flagged are in 'gateProblems'.",
  "Not re-run here: time-bot, foot-bot, search-bot, determinism-check (the last recorded determinism hashes are in docs/MAIN-BUILD.md sections 11-12). Blind 'newcomer' runs (a scripted first-time player, no hints, 2 attempts) are in bots/newcomer/: L1-5 only."
 ],
